    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "I think it's fair to say that there are many things on which I disagree with Rick Santorum, the former senator from Pennsylvania in a two-time presidential candidate. But I also have come to know him from our work as senior commentators for CNN. And while I still disagree with him on many, many things, I also found points of common concern that have been interesting to me. And I asked Rick in the wake of the Alabama election with all its consequences to sit down and talk about his life and career and where the Republican Party is today. And I think some of it may surprise you. I should say we're going to break from our normal format here and take an exchange that happened at the end of the conversation and move it up to the front of this podcast because I thought that the subject was so consequential that I didn't want anybody to miss it. So we're going to move that up and then get back to Senator Santorum's very interesting story. And I hope you'll stay on board for the entire journey. Rick Santoram, so good to be with you. It seems like just hours ago that we were sitting on a set talking about the election in Alabama and we'll get to that. We had this election in Alabama, followed an election in Virginia. There's something going on in the country. And there was something going on in 2016. I want you because you were sort of ahead of the curve in terms of cultural politics from the right. And also economic politics. You very much",
