    "turn_idx": 257,
    "turn_text": "Probably less so than than now. I think now there's a lot more currency. in, in doing that. I was, I was a little bit, I was, in some respects, you can say I may, may led, led the charge of me. I remember, you know, Robert Bird would always excoriate me for being, you know, for being, you know, talking like I was in a bar. And, and so I, again, I, I take full responsibility for all that. And, and, and some of the things, I, I don't regret having said, but a lot of them I do, and not what I said, but how I said it. And that matters, and I get that. And so, for me, part of what arked me in a different direction was the faith journey. And the second thing is, even through all those times, One of the things that I felt was that you have a responsibility to be there, not to just advance whatever cause you want to actually get something done. And so while people will say, you know, I was bombastic or controversial, I think if you look at the record of things that I actually accomplished in a bipartisan way, it's actually a fairly long and impressive list. And part of that was, in spite of the bombast, I take the example of Barbara Boxer and me. I mean, Barbara Boxer and I are probably former center from California is far away",
