    "turn_text": "Yeah, on contraception. And I find that, you know, I find that sort of disturbing, to be honest with you, that you'd be criticized for having a position that has been the position for the church for a couple thousand years and one that is not trying to impose that on to anybody else. the fact that we speak about I would recommend it does that threaten you potentially maybe you don't want to have this discussion but it but to me it was it was always sort of a to me a roose to say all you know Santor amis you know trying to impose controversy well I'm actually not but but I do believe it's it's something that if you look at what's happened since contraception has been there been some benefits clearly and there they've been documented but I think there also has been a a To me, a degradation of sexual relationships in this country, and I think you're seeing that through a lot of different things that are going on of how people treat each other when it comes to sexual activity. You're seeing it played out here with the sexual sex",
