  {
    "episode_id": 90460,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90460.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 340,
    "turn_text": "of my position because I actually approached this not from a religious point of view at all. In fact, when I decided to become pro-life, I'd never run for office and never really taken a position. I actually worked for a state senator who was pro-choice when I was out of graduate school. And so I'd sort of, I presume Heinz was too probably. Yeah, he was. And so to me it wasn't an important issue for me. I mean I was a young single guy and I never really thought much about it. But I was told, as I decided to run for office, that this was an important issue and I needed to get, so I went and I talked to some physicians. And they gave me some articles where I had a long dinner and walked through it. And to me, this was science. And scientifically, a life begins a conception. It's not a moral decision. It's a scientific fact. I mean, you have a unique DNA and that unique DNA is fully human and fully alive. So the question is, when do you want to give that human being, because it's human life, when do you want to give that human life right? And, you know, there's all sorts of gradations. Some people say, never, up until the moment that child was born. Some say, well, you know, after this one more weeks or after that number of weeks. But to me, from just using reason and logic, I said, well, you know, I don't think it's proper for the government to draw lines. And I certainly respect the liberty of a woman to have the right to do what she wants for their body. but nobody has the right of liberty to use that right of liberty to take another life. And so I put the right to life, which in our Declaration of Independence comes before the right to liberty, life liberty in the pursuit of happiness. I put that as a higher right. So that's how I came down. And so I know people say, well, it's a religious belief. Actually, it wasn't. Actually, it was just sort of this makes sense to me. And a society is probably a just society that puts life above liberty.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "A human life begins at conception based on biological evidence.",
        "confidence": 0.98
      },
      {
        "text": "I approached the pro-life position without a religious perspective.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "I had not previously held political positions on abortion prior to running for office.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "The genetic material present at conception constitutes a unique and fully human DNA sequence.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "I once worked for a pro-choice state senator after graduate school.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "No individual has the right to exercise bodily autonomy in a way that terminates another person’s life.",
