    "turn_text": "in so many cases and feeling abandoned and feeling misused and feeling vulnerable and alone. We'll bring that person in and we will care for her. We will provide support for her. And if she decides to move forward the pregnancy, we will support that pregnancy and care for her and her child, not just through the pregnancy, but afterwards in parenting and nurturing and all those things. And to me, that's the positive approach. Look, I don't think we should stop trying to change the law, which I believe is unjust. You can't just sit there and run your protest and as you said, scream at the other side and call the murderers or whatever the case may be. You have to go out and meet the women in society who are abandoned by men. parents, friends, in this very, very tragic, unwanted pregnancy situation. And so I think it's underreported, but I can tell you there are hundreds of these centers around the country, hundreds and hundreds. I've spoken at probably close to 100 myself and very, very passionate about being there to serve women and their children. And by the way, fathers trying to help with father and parenting. So to me, Yes, it's a very contentious debate.",
