    "turn_text": "And I would say this, that hopefully we can get some agreement. But the larger point here is those decisions are judgment decisions. They're complex. They have a lot of, you know, certain people we should probably should treat this way. Other people, we wouldn't treat this way. And it is up for the governmental official. And the church has to give leeway to that government official as long as they're doing it consistent with the teachings of the church, which is, you know, that we welcome the stranger and that we try to care for people. But at the same time, we can't welcome everybody. And I don't think any church teaches that you have to have an open border and everybody can come in. And nations have borders and they have boundaries. And it's a judgment",
